    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="text-body-secondary">Last updated: {{updated}}</p>
    <p><strong>In short:</strong> Wayhop is free and given as it is. We do our best to keep it right, but we can't promise it is. When it matters, check at the station or with OASA or STASY.</p>

    <h2>The information is given as it is</h2>
    <p>Wayhop shows times, arrivals, routes and station details as well as it can, but it can't promise that any of it is right, complete or up to date, or that Wayhop will be there when you need it. Buses run late, timetables change, lifts break down, and the services Wayhop relies on can stop answering.</p>

    <h2>Where it comes from</h2>
    <p>Most of it comes from OASA and STASY: live bus arrivals, timetables, announcements and lifts out of service. <a href="/about">About</a> lists every source. Wayhop collects some of it itself: which carriage to ride for an exit, which platforms you can reach without steps, ticket prices, and the facts on the Info page. Wayhop checks these as carefully as it can and says where something isn't confirmed yet, but they can still be wrong.</p>

    <h2>Check when it matters</h2>
    <p>If you're catching the last train, going to the airport or need step-free access, check the signs and announcements at the station, or {{#external href="https://www.stasy.gr/"}}STASY's{{/external}} and {{#external href="https://www.oasa.gr/"}}OASA's{{/external}} websites. Lifts can stop working at any time: {{#external href=stasyLifts}}STASY's elevator page{{/external}} shows which are out of service now. Wayhop links to that page wherever it says a platform can be reached without steps.</p>

    <h2>An independent project</h2>
    <p>Wayhop is not affiliated with or endorsed by OASA, STASY, OSY or any other transport operator. It can't help with tickets, refunds, lost property or complaints about a service; <a href="/contact">Contact</a> says who can.</p>

    <h2>Responsibility</h2>
    <p>You use Wayhop at your own risk. As far as the law allows, we are not responsible for any loss from using Wayhop or from not being able to use it, such as a missed connection or a trip that took longer. Nothing here takes away rights the law gives you that can't be waived.</p>

    <h2>Using Wayhop fairly</h2>
    <p>Wayhop is free and needs no account. Please don't use it in ways that harm it or the services behind it, such as sending it automated requests in bulk: everyone shares OASA's live data. Wayhop's code and the data collected for it are open, under the licences listed on <a href="/about">About</a>. Use those instead of the website.</p>

{{#if ads}}
    <h2>Ads</h2>
    <p>The ads come from Google. Wayhop doesn't choose them and doesn't vouch for what they advertise.</p>

{{/if}}
    <h2>Other websites</h2>
    <p>Wayhop links to other websites, such as OASA's, STASY's and Google Maps. We aren't responsible for what they contain, and their own terms apply there.</p>

    <h2>Law</h2>
    <p>Greek law applies to these terms. If you live elsewhere in the European Union, you keep the protection your own country's law gives you.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If these terms change, this page will show the new date. Questions: <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
</article>
